Package: QUESTIONS
Type: Package
Title: Quantifying Expression Spillover Trajectories in Omic Network Series
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Carly A.", "Bobak", email = "carly.a.bobak@dartmouth.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Jaini", "Shah", email = "jaini.h.shah.GR@dartmouth.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("A. James", "O'Malley", email = "james.omalley@dartmouth.edu", role = "aut"))
Description: Adapts the network-spillover (peer-exposure) decomposition from the
    analysis of interference in social networks to gene co-expression networks.
    Given a weighted network over genes, a module assignment, a per-unit quantity
    to propagate, and an outcome, QUESTIONS separates each module's own activity
    (a direct term) from the activity reaching it across between-module edges (a
    spillover term) and tests whether cross-module spillover predicts the outcome
    beyond direct activity, with small-sample validation (Freedman-Lane
    permutation with Benjamini-Hochberg adjustment, bootstrap confidence
    intervals and sign-stability, repeated cross-validation, and leave-one-out).
    Associations are correlational. Includes tested helpers for responsive-gene
    scoping and signed mutual-kNN plus Infomap network construction.
